<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19605" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάτᾰλος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βᾱ], ὁ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρωκτός</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				82
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάτας, βατέω.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>stammerer</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βατταρίζω</span>),
			a nickname given to Demosthenes, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				2.99
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.180
			</span></i>. (Codd. vary between <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάταλος</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάτταλος</span>:
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάτταλος</span> is pr. n. in <i><span class="en">
				Hedyl.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				4.167d
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>